WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.910
Welcome to SaleLedger. This short tour uses fictional practice files, so nothing here is a

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:13.821
real auction house. To begin, go to getsaleledger.com and click Start free month. Checkout

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:20.654
is handled by Stripe. A card is required, but nothing is charged for thirty days, and you

00:00:20.654 --> 00:00:22.420
can cancel before then.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:30.303
After checkout, you land on this page. It shows your license key. Copy it somewhere safe.

00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:37.086
We also keep it with your subscription, so you can come back to this page any time to see

00:00:37.086 --> 00:00:43.793
it again. The download button for the Windows installer is right below. Run it once, and

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:46.460
SaleLedger appears on your desktop.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:53.966
Double-click the SaleLedger icon on your desktop. It opens in your web browser, on your

00:00:53.966 --> 00:01:00.593
own computer. The first time, it asks you to read a short agreement: what SaleLedger does,

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:07.146
what stays your responsibility, and that your records never leave this computer. Tick the

00:01:07.146 --> 00:01:10.460
box and click I agree. You only do this once.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.927
Now paste your key and click Activate. That key is the only thing SaleLedger ever sends

00:01:17.927 --> 00:01:24.075
anywhere. Your ledger, your bank statement, and your consignor data never leave this

00:01:24.075 --> 00:01:24.660
machine.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:32.536
Each month you need three files. One: a settlement export from Auction Flex. The plain

00:01:32.536 --> 00:01:39.548
Consignor Summary, Consignment Order totals, or item-level totals all work; use whichever

00:01:39.548 --> 00:01:46.403
report you already run. Two: the QuickBooks IIF file that Auction Flex's Pay Consignors

00:01:46.403 --> 00:01:53.101
tool exports. Three: your trust account bank statement, as CSV, Excel, or your bank's

00:01:53.101 --> 00:01:54.440
Quicken download.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:02.156
Under Option A, choose the three files. Then enter the auction number, the trust account's

00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:08.624
opening balance on the first day of the period, and the as-of date. In the practice set,

00:02:08.624 --> 00:02:15.093
that's auction 246, an opening balance of one hundred fifty thousand dollars, and August

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:17.960
thirty-first. Click Run reconciliation.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:24.953
The result is one line: In balance, or Out of balance. Below it, the three numbers that

00:02:24.953 --> 00:02:30.914
have to agree: the bank's adjusted balance, the trust control balance from your records,

00:02:30.914 --> 00:02:36.876
and the total owed to consignors. In the practice month they don't agree, and the report

00:02:36.876 --> 00:02:38.840
says so instead of hiding it.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:46.218
Every gap becomes a numbered exception in plain English. Here, a consignor check cleared

00:02:46.218 --> 00:02:52.425
for five hundred dollars more than the ledger recorded. Further down, a deposit with no

00:02:52.425 --> 00:02:58.132
matching auction, and a transfer to the operating account with no authorization.

00:02:58.132 --> 00:03:03.340
SaleLedger never guesses at an explanation. It tells you what to look at.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:10.333
The report ends with a check register: date, check number, payee, and amount, taken

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:16.510
straight from your QuickBooks export. That is exactly what state bookkeeping rules like

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.930
Wisconsin's ask for.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:25.173
Above the report: save it as a file, export the numbers to a spreadsheet, print it or save

00:03:25.173 --> 00:03:31.044
it as a PDF, or email it to your bookkeeper. Keep a copy with the month's records, and

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.320
you're audit-ready without doing anything extra.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:42.295
Next month, SaleLedger pre-fills the opening balance from the bank's actual ending balance

00:03:42.295 --> 00:03:48.865
last period, so you never retype it. Bring in three new files, click Run, and read the

00:03:48.865 --> 00:03:52.990
result. That's the whole routine. Thanks for watching.
